 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Dark Claw — Innate Technique (6th level)</em></p><p>At 6th level, choose one of your Claw options to be replaced by its Upgraded Claw option. You gain an additional Upgraded Claw option at 11th and 18th level. You can have two Upgraded Claw options at a time and switch as part of short or long rest.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Brutal Claws</strong>. Your claws deal one additional damage dice on a hit and gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls. This increases to +3 at 11th level.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Elemental Claws</strong>. You can choose to change the damage type of your claws to one of the following types: fire, cold, lightning, thunder, acid. You deal additional damage equal to your proficiency bonus on a hit. You can change the damage type during a long rest.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Absorbing Claws</strong>. On a hit, you can spend 1 CE to deal an additional 2d6 necrotic damage. You regain hit points equal to the necrotic damage dealt. This increases to 3d6 at 11th level.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Pure Claws</strong>. Your claws ignore damage resistances and immunities. At 18th level, you deal maximum slashing damage against a creature without immunities or resistances to your damage.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Barbed Claws</strong>. Once per turn on a hit with your claws, you can spend 2 CE to force the target to make a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, they are bleeding and take 2d6 slashing damage at the start of their turn. This ends if the creature uses their action to staunch the wound or regains hit points.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
   "chat": ""
  },
